# Housing Query Implementation Record (English backup)

## Status

- Completed: 2026-09-24
- Scope: factual Housing Query foundation, PostGIS, API, read-only MCP and map integration
- Excluded: recommendation/ranking, booking, payment, public deployment and custom basemap
- Safety: no original OSM, PBF, OSRM graph or existing PostgreSQL data was modified

## Implemented Components

| Component | Location | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Shared contracts | `packages/contracts` | Zod schemas for place, route and housing |
| Query services | `packages/housing-query` | Hard SQL/PostGIS filters and bounded OSRM commute checks |
| Migrations | `database/migrations` | Schemas, roles, constraints, indexes and audit tables |
| POI importer | `platform-api/src/import-places.ts` | Versioned, traceable and duplicate-aware import |
| Platform API | `platform-api` | Seven local factual endpoints |
| MCP server | `mcp-server` | Six read-only `stdio` tools |
| Map integration | `map-app/src/services/platform-poi.ts` | City-bounded API loading with GeoJSON fallback |
| Operations | `Start-LifeFlow.ps1`, `Stop-LifeFlow.ps1` | Repeatable start and non-destructive stop |

## Database Isolation

The LifeFlow database runs in `lifeflow-postgis`:

```text
Host: 127.0.0.1
Port: 5433
Database: lifeflow
Volume: lifeflow-postgis-data
```

The pre-existing Windows PostgreSQL service on port `5432` was not changed.
Its credentials were not available, so it was intentionally not reset or
modified. The new LifeFlow database has its own logical backup:

```text
database/backups/lifeflow-20260924.dump
```

## Imported Data

| Metric | Value |
|---|---:|
| Source POI features | 13,120 |
| Canonical places | 13,118 |
| Duplicate source IDs | 2 |
| Rejected records | 0 |
| City boundaries | 3 |
| Production housing listings | 0 |

Every accepted canonical place keeps its OSM source ID, source payload and
import-run provenance. Housing remains empty because no real housing-listing
source exists in the workspace.

